Rafael -- agreed, say it up front. I'll write a paragraph for the
discussion framing BRF as the reference condition rather than a data point, a=
nd we
can show the specialist curve with and without it in Fig. S4.

I also want to check whether the specialist lag tracks bare-ground cover. Jon=
ah's
2019 quadrat data have percent bare ground at every pan-trap station. If grou=
nd
nesters are limited by nesting substrate rather than flowers, that's a manage=
ment
recommendation DNR can actually act on (prescribed burns open up bare ground).

-- M

